8. Bottom panel - Spreadsheet view
Shows the same data as main view but in spreadsheet form.
Allows user to select rows (images)
At the top of the spreadsheet, there are controls:
- checkbox: "selected only" (to only display rows corresponding to selected thumbnails)
- checkbox: "tagged only" (to only display rows where image is tagged for ingest)
- button: "version check" : will compare version from file with next available version in AYON and show warning if it is older.
- button: "untag lower version" untag rows with version lower than last version in AYON
- button: "select lower version" select rows with version lower than last version in AYON
- button: "check duplicates" : will check for duplicates with the same AYON path and the same label. It will only check the images that are tagged for ingest. Duplicates will be selected, rows will have red background.
- button: "invert tags" : will invert the tags of the selected images (toggle between tag and untag).
- button: "tag/untag selected" : will tag/untag all selected images

- Columns:
- Ingest checkbox (user editable)
- Small thumbnail preview
- Label (user editable, initially from filename)
- Version (user editable, initially from filename)
- Last Version in AYON
- AYON Path
- Age (in units from right panel filter)

- Sortable columns
- Allows user to and tag or untag images for ingest. (done by ingest checkbox)
- Allows user to edit the label in spreadsheet. The right click context menu in main window performs the same operations as the right click context menu in spreadsheet for label editing.
- Allows user to edit the version in spreadsheet by typing number
- Allows user to multi select rows by clicking the row number and using shift and ctrl keys.
- Allows user to select rows by clicking on the thumbnail - selects corresponding row

9. Ingest Button
Clicking the "Ingest" button will:
- "check duplicates" - same as in top panel. If duplicates found, ingest is stopped with message.
- "check versions" - same as in top panel. If older versions found, select them and show message - ingest is stopped with message.
- start ingest process. The ingest process will first create csv file with all the data required for AYON TrayPublisher CSV ingest
- The CSV is used by TrayPublisher to ingest the files into AYON - calling external process
- After TrayPublisher finishes, app will use AYON API to check if the files are in AYON and set the colors of the spreadsheet rows to bright green (ingested) or red (error) and show message to the user.




